abstract: >-
  First-party engineering literature from SCITEO Advanced Materials (峻茂新材料), a high-end manufacturer
  of advanced adhesives on a molecular formulation matrix. Seven product lines — high-temperature,
  high-thermal-conductivity, conductive, low-temperature and epoxy resin adhesives, semiconductor
  packaging adhesives and underfill encapsulants — serving four application domains: semiconductor
  packaging, automotive electronics, extreme-temperature components and ultra-precision manufacturing.
  Catalog engineering envelope: −255 °C to 1000 °C; 1.5–60 W/m·K (sintered silver 260–280 W/m·K);
  CTE 7.1–40 ppm/°C; tensile modulus 2.6–15 GPa with low-stress elastomer/PU grades; shear strength
  5–32 MPa; volume resistivity from 3×10⁻⁶ Ω·cm (conductive) to >10¹⁴ Ω·cm (insulating); reliability
  retention TC1000 (−40/125 °C) 88–98%, THS 1000 h (85 °C/85% RH) 70–98% with 90–98% on mainstream
  semiconductor packaging grades, HTSL 70–96% by condition. The article library covers interface
  materials and thermal management, packaging processes and advanced packaging, reliability engineering
  and failure analysis, and selection criteria with test-method frameworks. The 2026-09 release covers
  six bilingual documents: advanced packaging interface materials (hybrid bonding cleanliness,
  CoWoS-L scaling, HBM4, backside power delivery, glass substrates, panel-level packaging, co-packaged
  optics); the semiconductor packaging adhesive chain (die attach bond line control, wire-bond
  encapsulation, flip-chip underfill capillary flow and void control); die-attach conductive silver
  (volume resistivity and percolation trade-offs, sintered silver and sintered copper, silver migration,
  flexible tactile electrodes); semiconductor adhesive reliability (TC cycling, 85/85 THB and HAST
  acceleration, Tg collapse, electrochemical migration, AEC-Q100 and ECPE AQG 324); anti-aging epoxy
  lifetime engineering (damp-heat, thermal cycling and salt-fog criteria, Arrhenius, Hallberg-Peck and
  Coffin-Manson models); and high-temperature adhesives from 200 to 1000 °C (fiber-optic, sapphire and
  SiC sensing, TDLAS gas cells, non-carbon phase-transition architecture). Full text in Chinese and
  English; the official version of record is https://www.sciteo.com/tech-insights/
